  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p>Last updated: October 14, 2026</p>

  <p>
    This policy describes how the personal Rclone Personal Drive Mount
    setup accesses and handles Google Drive data.
  </p>

  <h2>Purpose and use of data</h2>
  <p>
    The owner uses rclone to access their Google Drive files from a
    privately managed home server. Google Drive access is used for
    personal file management and media-library access.
  </p>

  <h2>Google account authorization</h2>
  <p>
    Rclone uses Google's OAuth authorization mechanism to obtain
    permission to access the owner's Google Drive account.
    OAuth credentials and tokens are managed by rclone and stored
    in its local configuration on the owner's server.
    This website does not receive or store those credentials.
  </p>

  <h2>Storage and sharing</h2>
  <p>
    Files accessed through rclone may be cached on the owner's server,
    according to the owner's local configuration. Rclone communicates
    with Google services to perform the requested file operations.
    This website does not operate a backend that collects, processes,
    or shares Google Drive files.
  </p>

  <h2>Website data and cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This static website does not intentionally collect personal
    information, run analytics, or set tracking cookies. GitHub,
    as the website hosting provider, may process technical information
    associated with serving web pages under its own privacy practices.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    Google Drive and GitHub are third-party services subject to their
    respective terms and privacy policies. Data sent to Google through
    rclone is handled under Google's applicable policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For questions about this personal project, use the developer
    contact information shown on the Google OAuth consent screen.
  </p>

  <p><a href="./">Back to homepage</a></p>
